{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe driver explicitly denies any lifetime blackout, loss of consciousness or episode of impaired awareness, and the current nurse history confirms no blackout history; a sister's faint after standing in a hot room is recorded as family information, while the driver's own tiredness after an overnight route occurred with preserved awareness and no witness-reported unresponsiveness, rather than a confirmed episode being denied or reclassified after the fact.\n\nThe driver alternates urban deliveries with a longer motorway leg and describes a busy depot where engine noise, glare and interrupted meals can complicate an account of symptoms; the nurse records the work setting as context, while keeping the dated clinical findings distinct from the driver's explanation for why a symptom might have occurred on that shift.\n\nThe nurse reads the summary back to the driver to check the chronology and separates agreement about the wording from verification of a medical finding, then attaches the identified clinical material; any decision about further investigation or work allocation remains for the reviewing professional, and the note itself does not certify that all relevant clinical questions have been answered.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
